From: Ki-up KIM
Subject: [CCM] Mult-Origin Weekly Report - Week46

To : All Concerning L/OFCs
Cc : All Concerning Parties
Fm : CCM

We are grateful to all OFCs for a good feedback on the weekly Multi-origin report.

Please find the WK46 PFMC Vs. R/vol(Reference vol) by OFC & customer as attached.
All loading OFCs under 70%(in green) are kindly required to send reasons by Wednesday(Nov 20th).
RHQ Contract managers & HO are also requested to pay keen attention to reasons loading
OFCs get you.

We know that some customers have already headed into their slow season but TPE PFMC of
several customers such as Pantos, W/Mart, LG Sourcing, Goodyear & TOY "R" US falls
short of their average TPE vols for last 10 weeks(R/vol), so all concerning contract & loading PIC
are kindly requested to come up with reasons and take measures unless you anticipate any upswing
in near time.
For further details on their PFMC, please refer to # in green/boldface on the tap " WK46 PFMC
by ACCT " in the attachment.

FYR, please refer to notes below for the attachment.

 - The purpose of this report is to enhence the communication among loading & contract OFCs/RHQs.
 - R/Vol : not target but reference vols based on average Vol for last 10 weeks.
 - OFCs with PFMC ratio under 70%(Vs. R/Vol) are only supposed to be shown in green.

Thanks & B. RGDS

Kiup Kim
HJS SELCCM
02-3770-6595 (Office)
010-5120-0521 (Cell)
kimkiup@hanjin.com<mailto:kimkiup@hanjin.com>


